# Milestone: M5
# Covers: at (mytag.leave?) — tier-2 tag-leave event; subscriber fires when
#         OP_POP_TAG executes (normal exit and tag.stop() cascades); ordering
#         relative to tier-1 onleave clause (spec #3 §3.2).
#
# deferred: v1.x — tag.leave? events not implemented (T55 tag enter/leave emit hooks)
# matrix-row: tag-scope-events
#
# Reason:
#   Same blockers as tag_enter.chk.  Additionally, the ordering between tier-1
#   onleave and tier-2 leave-event subscribers is specified in spec #3 §4.3:
#   tier-1 fires first, then tier-2.  This ordering is verified in
#   test_tag_enter_leave.c.  The scripted fixture additionally requires
#   tag.stop() method dispatch (M4 dispatch path, already present).
#
# Activate when Tag.new() + leave-event wiring + body dispatch are complete.
#
# Urbiscript source (activate at T55 + T59 + M5-scratch-frame):
#   var t = Tag.new("scope");
#   var log = "";
#   at (t.leave?) Realm.log = Realm.log + "out";
#   t: { 1 } onleave { Realm.log = Realm.log + "tier1" };
#   log
#   --- expected output ---
#   [00000000] nil
#   [00000001] ""
#   [00000002] nil
#   [00000003] 1
#   [00000004] "tier1out"
